# Where the in-game AddOn List files this addon. Without a Category it lands
# under the catch-all at the bottom, which is where every addon that never set
# one ends up. The per-locale lines are the client's own category names, so a
# French or German client files it under its own word rather than the English
# one -- the addon's own translations are a separate thing and cover fewer
# languages than this does.
## Category: Chat
## Category-enUS: Chat
## Category-deDE: Chat
## Category-esES: Chat
## Category-esMX: Chat
## Category-frFR: Discussion
## Category-itIT: Chat
## Category-koKR: 대화
## Category-ptBR: Bate-papo
## Category-ruRU: Чат
## Category-zhCN: 聊天
## Category-zhTW: 對話

# Libraries
Libs\LibStub\LibStub.lua
Libs\CallbackHandler-1.0\CallbackHandler-1.0.lua
Libs\LibUIDropDownMenu\LibUIDropDownMenu.lua

# Core Lua
Locales.lua
SocialPlus.lua

#@do-not-package@
# Debug / testing tool: the /spsim friend-list simulator. This whole block is
# stripped by the packager and the file itself is in .pkgmeta's ignore list, so
# it loads from a git checkout but never ships in a CurseForge release. Both
# halves are required: dropping only the file would leave the packaged .toc
# pointing at something that isn't there.
SocialPlusSim.lua
#@end-do-not-package@
